{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is a repeat no-show dispute between the same rider and the same driver inside the 90-day window: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2, and the rider's own claim text confirms it is 'another dispute with the same driver'. Under POL-NS-09(c) a pattern of 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver is a mandatory escalation trigger, and escalation under that clause is terminal — the Judge issues no monetary ruling and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contested SGD 4.00 has not been taken: fare_breakdown shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, total_charged 4.00 with charged_at null and no waiting-time or platform fee attached. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case is held rather than collected or refunded, so escalation on the repeat-dispute trigger in POL-NS-09(c) is the only disposition on this record that stops the disputed cancellation fee being collected from the rider before a human has reviewed a pair who have now disputed no-shows twice in 90 days.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's own profile supports an adverse imputation against this rider: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so the rider-side abuse limb of POL-NS-09(d) is not met. rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (1) is a LIFETIME counter, and POL-GEN-01 fixes the trailing-window field no_show_disputes_30d as the one POL-NS-09(d) reads and forbids substituting the lifetime counter for it. The escalation therefore stands on the pair's repeat-dispute history between this rider and this driver under POL-NS-09(c), not on any imputation about this rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose at the outset that EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fired the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no traffic advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window. Its absence is itself citable on the rider's side: because no advisory exists, the driver cannot invoke POL-NS-06(i) to accumulate dwell across separate in-geofence intervals, and POL-NS-06 says in terms that a MISSING traffic_advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and that asserting the limb against a missing artifact triggers escalation rather than exonerating anyone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09110-01", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case is escalated to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09(c), and escalation is terminal — no money moves now, and the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is held rather than collected from the rider or refunded.\n\nWhy it escalates. The rider's point is the one that decides the case. rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2, and the rider's own filing confirms it is 'another dispute with the same driver'. That is 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days, which is a mandatory escalation trigger under POL-NS-09(c). The rider-side abuse limb, POL-NS-09(d), is NOT the ground: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (1) is a lifetime counter that limb (d) does not read and may not be substituted for. Escalation here holds the fee; it is not a rider win and not a driver win.\n\nOn the merits, the driver's no-show case is clean, and it is only the escalation trigger that stops it being paid out now. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold: (a) the trip record carries a driver arrival event at 2026-09-10T06:50:20+08:00; (b) the GPS trace places the driver 24.01 m from the pin from 06:50:00 — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and before the arrival timestamp; (c) the continuous in-geofence dwell, measured from the first qualifying fix and not from the arrival tap, is 330 seconds, 30 seconds beyond the 300-second STANDARD minimum; and (d) no boarding event is recorded and the driver terminated the trip at 06:55:30 — after the dwell elapsed — with code RIDER_NO_SHOW. Nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: the driver was inside the arrival radius, so POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance analysis is never reached; POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider because the driver replied in chat 20 seconds after the rider's message (well inside the 120-second window) and the rider's device never came within the 100 m presence radius (all 16 rider fixes sit about 519 m away); POL-NS-05 does not bite because the arrival marker was neither more than 300 m from the pin nor at 15 km/h (the trace is stationary at 0 km/h); and POL-NS-06 is not reached because there is no shortfall. On that basis the driver's compensation under POL-NS-07 would be SGD 3.20 (80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, which reconciles under POL-NS-08(d) to the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee), and the anti-farming check does not withhold it — 1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips is neither 4 or more nor above a 0.08 rate. That entitlement is recorded for the reviewer, but it cannot be paid while the case is escalated, so both money fields are null.\n\nImpaired evidence, disclosed and weighed: EV-ADVIS-09110-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. It can carry no fact, no finding relies on it, and it therefore does not move the confidence cap; POL-NS-06(i) is simply unavailable (though POL-NS-06 is not reached in any event). The fare is otherwise clean and no POL-NS-08 limb is engaged — the arrival event falls on the trace's 10-second cadence with no skew, the trace has no gap over 120 seconds and 34 fixes across the window, and the chat log's 4 messages match the trip record with no missing msg_id or five-minute gap.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: given that the driver's no-show case is fully established on the merits, but this rider and this driver have now disputed no-shows twice in 90 days, decide whether that repeat pattern indicates abuse on either side and how the disputed SGD 4.00 fee should finally be disposed of — held, refunded to the rider, or released to the driver together with the SGD 3.20 POL-NS-07 compensation."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
